>> servings: 4

Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Mince the @garlic{2%cloves}. Zest and juice one @lemon{1} and thinly slice another @lemon{1}. Chop the @red onion{1} into thick wedges. Finely chop the @dill{2%tbsp} and @parsley{2%tbsp}, plus extra of each for garnish. Chop the @lebanese cucumber{2}. Slice the @lime{1} into wedges. Trim the fat from the @chicken thighs{500%g}.

In a medium bowl, combine @greek yoghurt{140%g}, 1 tbsp extra virgin olive oil, the garlic, lemon zest and juice, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, @paprika{1%tsp}, @ground turmeric{0.5%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, @sumac{0.5%tsp}, @chilli flakes{0.5%tsp}, salt and black pepper. Stir well, then add the chicken thighs and coat evenly.

Arrange the onion wedges and lemon slices on a baking tray, drizzle with a little olive oil, and sprinkle with a pinch of salt. Place the marinated chicken on top. Roast for ~{22.5%minutes}, or until the chicken is cooked through.

In a small bowl, combine @greek yoghurt{140%g}, the juice of @lemon{0.5}, the chopped dill and parsley, and a pinch of salt. Set aside.

Remove the chicken from the oven and garnish with the cucumber, extra dill and parsley, dollops of the herbed yoghurt, and lime wedges. Serve with @cooked rice{} or @pita{}.
